<title>CANADA: NHL ICE HOCKEY-LIST OF MAJOR END OF SEASON AWARD WINNERS.</title>
<headline>NHL ICE HOCKEY-LIST OF MAJOR END OF SEASON AWARD WINNERS.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>List of the National Hockey</p>
<p>League's annual end of season awards and the winners who were</p>
<p>named on Thursday.</p>
<p>Hart Memorial Trophy (Most Valuable Player)</p>
<p>Dominik Hasek (Buffalo Sabres)</p>
<p>Norris Trophy (Top defenceman)</p>
<p>Brian Leetch (New York Rangers)</p>
<p>Vezina Trophy (Top goaltender)</p>
<p>Dominik Hasek (Buffalo Sabres)</p>
<p>Frank J. Selke Trophy (Best defensive forward)</p>
<p>Michael Peca (Buffalo Sabres)</p>
<p>Calder Trophy (Rookie of the Year)</p>
<p>Bryan Berard (New York Islanders)</p>
<p>Jack Adams Award (Coach of the Year)</p>
<p>Ted Nolan (Buffalo Sabres)</p>
<p>Lady Byng Trophy (Sportsmanship and gentlemanly conduct)</p>
<p>Paul Kariya (Anaheim Mighty Ducks)</p>
<p>Lester B. Pearson Award (MVP in voting by players)</p>
<p>Dominik Hasek (Buffalo Sabres)</p>
<p>Art Ross Trophy (Regular season scoring champion)</p>
<p>Mario Lemieux (Pittsburgh Penguins)</p>
